        "original_id": "75c81a02-6add-5bf9-a34a-0e5ff1c589d7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Cardillac, La donna del lago\n- People: Paul Hindemith, Gioachino Rossini, Andrea Leone Tottola, Sir Walter Scott\n- Concepts: opera, libretto, The Lady of the Lake\n\nFacts:\n- In 1810, Sir Walter Scott wrote the narrative poem The Lady of the Lake.\n- Sir Walter Scott's The Lady of the Lake helped popularize the image of the romantic Highlands.\n- Cardillac is an opera by Paul Hindemith in three acts and four scenes.\n- La donna del lago is an opera composed by Gioachino Rossini.\n- La donna del lago has a libretto by Andrea Leone Tottola.\n- One critic described Andrea Leone Tottola's verses for La donna del lago as limpid.\n- La donna del lago is based on the French translation of Sir Walter Scott's The Lady of the Lake.",
